# Pin installs to the public npm registry.
#
# This repository is public and its CI runs on GitHub-hosted runners, which
# have no access to any corporate mirror. Without this, running `npm install`
# on a machine configured with an internal registry rewrites the `resolved`
# URLs in package-lock.json to that internal host. The lockfile still installs
# fine locally, so the breakage is invisible until CI (or an outside
# contributor) tries `npm ci` and gets ECONNREFUSED.
#
# That is exactly what happened: 13 jszip-related entries pointed at an
# internal artifact proxy and broke every CI run.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
